    {
      "slug": "good-form",
      "title": "Good Form",
      "year": 2022,
      "categories": [
        "editorial"
      ],
      "location": "São Paulo",
      "description": "Boa Forma / Gute Form – Design in Brazil 1947–1968 explores the connections, schools and exhibitions that shaped the exchange between modern design in Brazil and Germany. The challenge was to make a complex network of historical references, people and events accessible while preserving its richness and context. Through archival research, the design of infographics and timelines, and a cohesive editorial structure, the book translates these connections into a clear visual narrative. I led the creative direction and design of the entire publication, from concept to production.",
      "credits": "Creative Direction & Design – Ilana Tschiptschin, Julio Mariutti",
