      "description": "Graciliano Ramos: A Ética da Escrita (2013) was an exhibition dedicated to the life and work of Brazilian writer Graciliano Ramos, presented at the Paraty Literary Festival. The challenge was to translate a literary archive into an immersive spatial experience, allowing visitors to engage with the writer’s words beyond the traditional exhibition format. The solution was an installation of 650 individually printed A4 cards suspended throughout the space, transforming texts into a spatial composition and blurring the boundaries between archive, literature and exhibition. The project received an award at the 11th Brazilian Graphic Design Biennial.",
